\end_layout

\end_inset

 (accessed on 20 June 2026).
 For the feature construction process used in the FC2(RF) and FC2(MLP) algorithms,
 we utilized the freely available programming tool QFc
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "QFC"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 accessible at 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://github.com/itsoulos/QFc
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (accessed on 20 June 2026).
 In addition,
 the GENCLASS 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "GenClass 2021"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 system was employed in our experiments.
 GENCLASS is a free software framework entirely written in ANSI C++,
 available by 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://github.com/itsoulos/GenClass/
\end_layout

\end_inset

(accessed on 20 June 2026) designed to construct classification programs in a C like programming language for the purpose of classifying input data.
 It operates as an evolutionary rule induction method,
 generating interpretable decision rules through genetic search mechanisms.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each experiment was executed 30 times,
 using different seeds for the random number generator in every run.
 In addition,
 the ten\SpecialChar nobreakdash
fold cross\SpecialChar nobreakdash
validation procedure was applied to ensure robust validation of the experimental results.
 The proposed feature construction method was applied independently to each fold,
 and the average classification errors on the corresponding test sets were computed.
 For the experimental tables the following notation was used:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The column DATASET denotes the dataset corresponding to a regions where the machine learning methods were applied.
 Attica contains 1.859 records,
 of which 844 correspond to class 0 and 1.015 to class 1.
 Eastern Macedonia & Thrace contains 2.653 records,
 of which 1.093 correspond to class 0 and 1.559 to class 1.
 Crete contains 2.789 records,
 of which 1.383 correspond to class 0 and 1.404 to class 1.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The column MLP(BFGS) represents the application of an artificial neural network 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "nn1,nn2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 with 10 processing nodes trained with the BFGS optimization method 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "powell"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The column RBF stands for the usage of a Radial Basis Function (RBF) network 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "rbf1,rbf2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 with 10 processing nodes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The column RF denotes the application of the Random Forest model 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "random_forest"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
